00:36:54.410 --> 00:36:56.310
quite selfish and self-involved.
是相当自私和以自我为中心的。

1011
00:36:56.430 --> 00:37:02.630
But I remember dropping my daughter, sometimes dropping my daughter off to school in America,
但我记得有几次送我女儿去学校，在美国，

1012
00:37:02.870 --> 00:37:04.670
in Los Angeles, and we were living there.
在洛杉矶，当时我们住在那里。

1013
00:37:04.810 --> 00:37:06.270
And my mom was living with me.
我妈妈也和我住在一起。

1014
00:37:06.470 --> 00:37:08.950
She'd moved over and everything was good.
她搬了过来，一切都很好。

1015
00:37:09.090 --> 00:37:12.810
And I remember then going, and now I'm going to go and work on The Office.
我记得当时心想，现在我要去拍《办公室》了。

1016
00:37:13.170 --> 00:37:18.290
And I just remember having a really crystallized moment of gratitude and appreciation.
我清楚地记得那一刻心中充满了感激和欣赏。

1017
00:37:18.810 --> 00:37:24.470
And it's kind of, because the show is so loved by people, you can dip into that every day,
这很特别，因为这部剧深受观众喜爱，你每天都能沉浸在这种感觉里，

1018
00:37:24.630 --> 00:37:24.870
can't you?
不是吗？

1019
00:37:24.950 --> 00:37:30.850
Because you go, oh my God, for a tiny little part and coasting on the coattails of all of
因为你会想，天哪，我只是参与了一个小角色，借着你们所有人的光，

1020
00:37:30.850 --> 00:37:33.530
you people that were there and set up and everything.
是你们奠定了基础，成就了一切。

1021
00:37:33.670 --> 00:37:38.250
And I was so privileged and honored to just come in and coast on the coattails of this
我感到非常荣幸和幸运，能加入这部精彩的剧集，

1022
00:37:38.250 --> 00:37:40.130
fantastic show with this fantastic caSt.
与这群出色的演员共事。

1023
00:37:40.310 --> 00:37:44.730
But I used to really just go, it was one of those pinch me moments because it was the
但我过去真的会想，那真是那种让人想掐自己一下确认是否在做梦的时刻，因为这是

1024
00:37:44.730 --> 00:37:47.790
only time I've ever watched a show and then been in it.
我唯一一次先看了某部剧，然后又参演了它。

1025
00:37:47.790 --> 00:37:51.610
Watched a show, loved it, been obsessed by it and then been in it.
看过这部剧，喜欢它，沉迷于它，然后又成为了它的一部分。

1026
00:37:51.710 --> 00:37:53.670
And you don't, that kind of doesn't often happen.
这种事通常不会发生。

1027
00:37:53.810 --> 00:37:53.990
Yeah.
是啊。

1028
00:37:54.230 --> 00:37:54.510
You know?
你知道吗？

1029
00:37:54.670 --> 00:38:00.210
And so I guess I've brought away this tiny little piece of being part of something so
所以我猜我带走了一小块碎片，那就是成为比我个人职业生涯

1030
00:38:00.210 --> 00:38:03.110
much bigger than my own career.
宏大得多的事物的一部分。

1031
00:38:03.110 --> 00:38:03.870
You know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

1032
00:38:03.910 --> 00:38:06.570
That I'm a tiny little part in this institution.
我只是这个机构中微不足道的一小部分。

1033
00:38:06.970 --> 00:38:09.490
And so that's a kind of more philosophical thing.
所以这是一种更哲学层面的感悟。

1034
00:38:09.610 --> 00:38:10.730
I didn't nick anything.
我没顺走任何东西。

1035
00:38:10.890 --> 00:38:11.850
I didn't steal anything.
我什么都没偷。

1036
00:38:11.930 --> 00:38:12.970
You didn't take anything at the end?
你最后什么都没拿吗？

1037
00:38:12.970 --> 00:38:17.590
Oh, and I listened to you all and you're going, we took so much stuff and Phyllis didn't get
哦，我听你们说，你们拿了好多东西，菲利斯甚至没拿到

1038
00:38:17.590 --> 00:38:19.430
her best bushiest beaver thing.
她那个最毛茸茸的海狸摆件。

1039
00:38:19.650 --> 00:38:19.810
Oh, yeah.
哦，是啊。

1040
00:38:20.010 --> 00:38:21.490
But I didn't take anything.
但我确实什么都没拿。

1041
00:38:21.870 --> 00:38:21.970
Nothing?
什么都没拿？

1042
00:38:22.270 --> 00:38:22.870
I took nothing.
我什么都没拿。

1043
00:38:22.870 --> 00:38:23.690
But you know what?
但你知道吗？

1044
00:38:23.890 --> 00:38:26.050
I found this out about two years ago.
我大约两年前才发现这件事。

1045
00:38:26.370 --> 00:38:33.090
They did some job lot, I guess, auctioned stuff from the props, right?
他们好像把道具打包拍卖了，对吧？

1046
00:38:33.250 --> 00:38:33.370
Yeah.
是啊。

1047
00:38:33.370 --> 00:38:39.670
One of the things they were selling was my notebook, I guess.
他们拍卖的东西里好像有我的笔记本。

1048
00:38:40.250 --> 00:38:43.310
Like a notebook from Nellie's desk notebook.
就是奈莉桌上的那种笔记本。

1049
00:38:44.190 --> 00:38:46.010
But did it have your real scribbles in it?
那上面有你真正的涂鸦吗？

1050
00:38:46.130 --> 00:38:46.430
Yes.
有的。

1051
00:38:46.650 --> 00:38:48.130
It had my real scribbles in it.
上面还有我真实的涂鸦。

1052
00:38:50.330 --> 00:38:51.850
And it had on it.
而且上面写着东西。

1053
00:38:52.250 --> 00:38:55.210
And because we went online and looked, because I was like, oh, my God, you better.
因为我们上网查了，当时我心想，天哪，你最好买下来。

1054
00:38:55.330 --> 00:38:56.770
I said to my husband, you better buy that.
我对丈夫说，你最好把它买下来。

1055
00:38:57.150 --> 00:39:01.130
Because can you imagine if I'm going, I'm so bored.
因为你能想象吗，如果我当时说，我太无聊了。

1056
00:39:01.950 --> 00:39:05.800
I didn't know what I was going to say.
我根本不知道自己要说什么。

1057
00:39:06.560 --> 00:39:07.980
And we looked online.
于是我们上网查了。

1058
00:39:08.680 --> 00:39:09.800
And do you know what?
你猜怎么着？

1059
00:39:09.920 --> 00:39:13.400
One of the things we could zoom in and see was an address.
我们放大后能看到的东西之一，是一个地址。

1060
00:39:13.940 --> 00:39:14.560
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1061
00:39:14.800 --> 00:39:15.860
It was an address.
那是一个地址。

1062
00:39:16.380 --> 00:39:17.340
And do you know what it was?
你猜那是哪儿？

1063
00:39:17.680 --> 00:39:20.840
It was the place of our first date.
那是我们第一次约会的地方。

1064
00:39:21.520 --> 00:39:21.880
What?
什么？

1065
00:39:22.120 --> 00:39:22.880
Isn't that crazy?
这难道不疯狂吗？

1066
00:39:23.660 --> 00:39:25.340
Like you had written it.
就像是你写上去的一样。

1067
00:39:25.460 --> 00:39:26.220
I'd written down.
我写下来的。

1068
00:39:26.360 --> 00:39:27.660
And this is when we were friends.
那时我们还是朋友。

1069
00:39:27.920 --> 00:39:28.940
We were just friends.
我们只是朋友。

1070
00:39:29.100 --> 00:39:30.000
I shouldn't say date.
我不该说是约会。

1071
00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:33.640
But I remember the time and him going, oh, do you want to?
但我记得当时他问我，你想去吗？

1072
00:39:33.760 --> 00:39:34.400
Because he's a writer.
因为他是个作家。

1073
00:39:34.540 --> 00:39:36.000
And I was like, oh, I'm writing this show.
我说，噢，我正在写这个节目。

1074
00:39:36.120 --> 00:39:36.680
Do you want to do it?
你想参与吗？

1075
00:39:36.700 --> 00:39:39.820
Because he was a dad from the school and blah, blah, blah.
因为他是学校里的一位家长，诸如此类的。

1076
00:39:40.980 --> 00:39:43.900
And I remember we met at this Tex-Mex place.
我记得我们在那家德州墨西哥餐厅见面。

1077
00:39:44.600 --> 00:39:45.820
And I still didn't eat a taco.
我当时还是没吃塔可。

1078
00:39:47.980 --> 00:39:49.140
I was like, I'll have a salad.
我说，我吃沙拉就行。

1079
00:39:49.380 --> 00:39:50.980
But that is so amazing.
但这真是太神奇了。

1080
00:39:51.180 --> 00:39:52.520
That's that moment in time.
那是那一刻的时光定格。

1081
00:39:52.520 --> 00:39:56.720
It had the Tex-Mex address at like 8 p.m.
上面写着晚上8点左右在德州墨西哥餐厅的地址。

1082
00:39:57.380 --> 00:39:58.460
Isn't that funny?
这难道不好笑吗？

1083
00:39:58.700 --> 00:40:01.260
That is so crazy.
这太疯狂了。

1084
00:40:01.760 --> 00:40:02.700
Did you get the book?
你买到那本书了吗？

1085
00:40:02.700 --> 00:40:03.120
Your first meeting.
你们第一次见面的地方。

1086
00:40:03.560 --> 00:40:03.960
No.
没有。

1087
00:40:04.560 --> 00:40:06.240
He wouldn't bid enough for it.
他出价不够高。

1088
00:40:08.520 --> 00:40:13.100
Were you surprised when you came on the show how much background work we had to do?
你刚来这个节目时，有没有对我们需要做的背景工作量感到惊讶？

1089
00:40:13.220 --> 00:40:15.900
How much you had to sit in the background of other people's stuff?
你得在别人的戏份里做背景板坐那么久？

1090
00:40:15.940 --> 00:40:16.160
Oh, my God.
噢，天哪。

1091
00:40:16.300 --> 00:40:16.420
Yes.
是的。

1092
00:40:16.420 --> 00:40:17.480
Did anyone warn you?
有人提醒过你吗？

1093
00:40:17.700 --> 00:40:18.200
No.
没有。

1094
00:40:18.640 --> 00:40:19.960
I did not know.
我完全不知道。

1095
00:40:20.220 --> 00:40:21.760
We were there all the time.
我们一直都在那儿。

1096
00:40:22.160 --> 00:40:22.620
All the time.
一直都在。

1097
00:40:22.620 --> 00:40:24.940
But of course, that's what made the show.
但当然，正是这一点成就了这部剧。

1098
00:40:25.180 --> 00:40:28.880
Because we felt like we lived there and we worked there and we were these people.
因为我们感觉自己就住在那里，在那里工作，我们就是这些人。

1099
00:40:29.340 --> 00:40:33.940
And actually, it would have been such a different experience if all you did was these isolated scenes.
说实话，如果只是拍那些孤立的场景，体验会完全不同。

1100
00:40:34.160 --> 00:40:34.480
Oh, for sure.
噢，那肯定的。

1101
00:40:34.740 --> 00:40:36.280
It would have just not been the same.
那感觉肯定完全不一样了。

1102
00:40:36.400 --> 00:40:37.980
But at the time, it was literally.
但在当时，确实就是那样。

1103
00:40:38.220 --> 00:40:41.100
And because a lot of the time I was with Stanley and Phyllis.
而且因为我大部分时间都和斯坦利还有菲利斯在一起。

1104
00:40:41.240 --> 00:40:41.400
Yeah.
是啊。

1105
00:40:41.740 --> 00:40:45.400
And I remember her saying, which is true, you know, she always used to have her signs in her desk.
我记得她说的一句话，确实如此，你知道，她以前总是在办公桌上放些标语。

1106
00:40:45.840 --> 00:40:46.600
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊，是啊。

1107
00:40:47.200 --> 00:40:51.160
And they would always, they would get me into these habits of going,
她们总是会让我养成一些习惯，比如去……

1108
00:40:51.160 --> 00:40:54.600
and just, you know, just put the sweets in your desk, the candy.
就是，你知道，把糖果放在你的办公桌里。

1109
00:40:54.720 --> 00:40:55.020
Yes.
没错。

1110
00:40:55.660 --> 00:40:56.300
In your desk.
在你的办公桌里。

1111
00:40:56.840 --> 00:40:58.600
And they'd fill up their thing with Coke.
她们会把自己的抽屉塞满可乐。

1112
00:40:59.020 --> 00:40:59.200
Yeah.
是啊。

1113
00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:04.980
I would go over to Phyllis's desk, open her drawer, look at her sides and grab a Tootsie Roll.
我会走到菲利斯的办公桌前，打开她的抽屉，看看她的剧本，然后抓一块图西卷糖。

1114
00:41:05.120 --> 00:41:05.380
Right.
对。

1115
00:41:05.540 --> 00:41:06.140
Right, right, right.
对，对，对。

1116
00:41:07.060 --> 00:41:08.240
Oh, so good.
哦，太棒了。

1117
00:41:08.460 --> 00:41:09.080
Yeah, so good.
是啊，太棒了。

1118
00:41:09.180 --> 00:41:14.220
And I guess, yeah, the other thing I took from the office was what I didn't expect when I left the office
我想，是的，我从办公室带走的另一件东西，是我离开办公室时没想到的，

1119
00:41:14.220 --> 00:41:19.820
was that I have an American life now because I met my husband, not at the office,
那就是我现在拥有了美国式的生活，因为我遇到了我的丈夫，虽然不是在办公室认识的，

1120
00:41:19.940 --> 00:41:22.680
but I met my husband because I was over here living.
但我遇到我丈夫是因为我当时住在这边。

1121
00:41:22.840 --> 00:41:23.480
During that time.
在那段时间里。

1122
00:41:23.640 --> 00:41:24.280
During that time.
在那段时间里。

1123
00:41:24.360 --> 00:41:24.460
Yeah.
是啊。

1124
00:41:24.640 --> 00:41:26.660
And it wasn't until, you know, years later we got together.
直到多年以后，我们才走到了一起。

1125
00:41:26.660 --> 00:41:31.080
But had I not got that job and lived in that place and my daughter gone to that school.
但如果我没有得到那份工作，没有住在那儿，我女儿也没有去那所学校上学的话……

1126
00:41:31.500 --> 00:41:31.760
Yeah.
是啊。

1127
00:41:32.080 --> 00:41:32.500
Crazy.
太疯狂了。

1128
00:41:33.080 --> 00:41:33.480
Yeah.
是啊。

1129
00:41:33.820 --> 00:41:34.440
It's meant to be.
这就是命中注定。

1130
00:41:34.580 --> 00:41:35.000
I know.
我知道。

1131
00:41:35.360 --> 00:41:35.920
It's meant to be.
这就是命中注定。

1132
00:41:36.460 --> 00:41:38.640
Angela, do you want to ask your call sheet questions?
安吉拉，你想问你的通告单问题了吗？

1133
00:41:38.840 --> 00:41:39.400
I do.
我想问。

1134
00:41:39.620 --> 00:41:40.880
I love them so much.
我太喜欢这些问题了。

1135
00:41:41.060 --> 00:41:42.340
So here we go.
那我们开始吧。

1136
00:41:42.560 --> 00:41:42.720
Okay.
好的。

1137
00:41:43.040 --> 00:41:46.960
Number one, what was your first entertainment job?
第一个问题，你的第一份演艺工作是什么？

1138
00:41:47.480 --> 00:41:49.160
Meaning the one I got paid for.
是指我有报酬的那一份吗？

1139
00:41:50.100 --> 00:41:50.540
Sure.
当然。

1140
00:41:50.760 --> 00:41:50.860
Sure.
当然。

1141
00:41:51.020 --> 00:41:53.160
Or just the one I found most entertaining.
还是指我最觉得有趣的那一份？

1142
00:41:53.640 --> 00:41:54.820
Your first one.
你的第一份工作。

1143
00:41:54.820 --> 00:41:56.520
What springs to mind.
想到什么就说什么。

1144
00:41:56.840 --> 00:42:04.220
I think it would have been on a show before I went to college and it was a sitcom called
我想那应该是在我上大学之前的一部剧，是一部情景喜剧，叫作

1145
00:42:04.960 --> 00:42:05.800
Surgical Spirit.
《外科医生精神》。

1146
00:42:06.460 --> 00:42:06.880
Oh.
哦。

1147
00:42:07.240 --> 00:42:08.800
And I was someone's girlfriend.
我在里面演某人的女朋友。

1148
00:42:09.100 --> 00:42:11.440
Like the mom in it had a son and I was his girlfriend.
就像剧里的妈妈有个儿子，我演他女朋友。

1149
00:42:11.720 --> 00:42:15.000
I think that's the thing I would have got my first paycheck from.
我想那应该是我拿到第一笔工资的工作。

1150
00:42:15.440 --> 00:42:16.600
And how old were you?
那你当时多大？

1151
00:42:16.760 --> 00:42:18.280
I would have been like 18.
那时我大概18岁吧。

1152
00:42:18.700 --> 00:42:19.240
Oh, wow.
噢，哇。

1153
00:42:19.340 --> 00:42:23.000
And did you already know entertainment was what you wanted to do with your life at that point?
那时候你已经确定自己这辈子想从事演艺事业了吗？

1154
00:42:23.000 --> 00:42:26.440
I definitely did because I deferred a year when I got into drama school.
我非常确定，因为我考上戏剧学校后还申请了延期入学一年。

1155
00:42:26.680 --> 00:42:30.300
So I had a whole year before I knew I was going and this was the summer before.
所以我有一整年的时间，那是在我去学校之前的那个夏天。

1156
00:42:30.560 --> 00:42:34.760
So I like walked into college with like TV credit.
所以我进大学的时候，就已经有电视节目的演出经验了。

1157
00:42:34.960 --> 00:42:35.280
Yeah.
是啊。

1158
00:42:35.440 --> 00:42:36.420
I've been on the television.
我上过电视了。

1159
00:42:38.200 --> 00:42:39.100
Did you even?
真的吗？

1160
00:42:39.180 --> 00:42:40.040
You barely needed.
你几乎都不需要（去上学）了。

1161
00:42:40.160 --> 00:42:40.380
Right.
没错。

1162
00:42:40.560 --> 00:42:41.940
I mean, what can you tell me?
我是说，你还能告诉我什么呢？

1163
00:42:42.180 --> 00:42:42.400
Yeah.
是啊。

1164
00:42:42.680 --> 00:42:43.340
I've done it all.
我什么都做过了。

1165
00:42:43.380 --> 00:42:44.260
In your three year course.
在你那三年的课程里。

1166
00:42:45.480 --> 00:42:46.040
All right.
好吧。

1167
00:42:46.200 --> 00:42:46.820
Next question.
下一个问题。

1168
00:42:46.980 --> 00:42:48.900
Do you speak any other languages?
你会说其他语言吗？

1169
00:43:00.680 --> 00:43:02.220
Oh, that was wonderful.
噢，那太棒了。

1170
00:43:02.780 --> 00:43:04.480
How did you come to speak so many languages?
你是怎么学会这么多语言的？

1171
00:43:04.840 --> 00:43:05.840
Well, do you know what it was?
嗯，你知道是怎么回事吗？

1172
00:43:05.920 --> 00:43:10.220
I think it comes back to wanting to be an actor because I realized I like to do voices.
我觉得这归结于我想成为一名演员，因为我意识到我喜欢模仿各种声音。

1173
00:43:10.660 --> 00:43:17.360
And I also realized that I was able to pick up languages very quickly because I was able to imitate the accent quite quickly.
而且我也发现自己能很快学会语言，因为我能很快模仿出那种口音。

1174
00:43:17.360 --> 00:43:25.280
It boosted me because people thought I could speak better than I could and it boosted me to do better actually than I did.
这对我很有帮助，因为人们会觉得我比实际说得更好，这反而促使我表现得比实际水平更好。

1175
00:43:25.460 --> 00:43:31.220
